{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ey7ccwn2u4v3qbx5kzsev7dc524khs4gqdbfuo3mjwottqzejgga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases are complete and independently verified.\n\n## Result: the Rust translation is correct — no fixes were needed\n\n`src/lib.rs` is byte-for-byte identical to the original translation (`diff` confirms), because every differential test passed against it.\n\n**Phase A — surface mapped** (all derived mechanically from the C, all three files on disk):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` (105 lines) — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol, `T sieve`; Rust `.so` exports it too. Missing-symbol diff **empty** in both dev and release profiles; `ldd -r` clean. Nothing was left untranslated (`c_src` is one 40-line translation unit).\n- `ERRORS.md` (11 rows) — the grep showed the C has **zero** explicit rejections (no `return`, `assert`, NULL check, error code, or range check), so the rows are the *implicit* ones: the truncating-`%` loop predicate, the discarded `printf` return, the unguarded `val++` overflow, the domain extremes, and the FFI boundaries.\n- `CONFIGS.md` (19 rows + axis table) — residue class × sign × magnitude × digit-width × stdout destination × call sequencing.\n\n**Phase B/C/D** — 33 tests in `tests/` load **both** `.so`s with `libloading` (`dlopen`/`dlsym` on `sieve`, never a direct Rust call) and compare raw stdout bytes: 18 valid-path (randomized, fixed-seed), 11 error-path, 4 symbol/parity. All pass single-threaded and in parallel, in dev **and** release (`panic = \"abort\"`). Cargo.toml declares no `[features]`, so the one valid combination is `--no-default-features`, enumerated and run by `verify_all.sh`.\n\nTwo findings worth flagging:\n\n1. **A stale-artifact trap that made verification worthless at first.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` target, so the suite was comparing against an outdated `.so` — I proved this by mutating the Rust to floor-mod (`rem_euclid`) and watching all tests still pass. The harness now uses the cargo artifact only when it is newer than `src/lib.rs`, otherwise compiles a fresh cdylib with `rustc`, and `d3_artifact_under_test_is_fresh` guards it permanently.\n2. **Harness sensitivity was then validated by mutation** (`mutation_check.sh`): 10 deliberate defects — floor-mod, `saturating_add`, check-before-print, print `val+1`, missing `\\n`, residue 8, step 2, `%u`, `%ld`, renamed export — were **all** detected (the non-terminating one as a loud timeout). Runs are executed in byte-capped, time-limited forked children so a divergent implementation fails instead of hanging or filling the disk.\n\nThe trickiest C behaviours are pinned down explicitly: C's `%` truncates toward zero, so negative starts can never match `9` and count all the way up (a floor-mod translation is caught by 9 tests); `INT_MAX`-range starts overflow (UB) and the shipped build wraps to `INT_MIN` — I checked this wrap is identical at `-O0` *and* `-O2`, and compare an 8 KiB prefix of those ~2^31-line runs; and the ignored `printf` failure is compared via `waitpid` status with stdout on `/dev/full` and on a closed fd, so \"returns normally\" is an observed fact rather than an assumption."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1272,"cache_read_input_tokens":139137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1272,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bd36f9b-9b34-4b47-afdd-5254c45236ff","uuid":"3bd831b1-58c2-4c76-923f-a02ee16611ff","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:52:02.136Z"}
